        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Luke</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>The Magnificat — &#x27;My soul doth magnify the Lord&#x27; — is for Cyril the first prophetic hymn of the New Covenant, spoken by the very mouth that bears the Word. Mary magnifies not by adding anything to God but by uniquely participating in his self-giving: she &#x27;magnifies&#x27; the Lord precisely as the bearer of his enfleshment. Cyril reads the song as the OT prophetic genre — the canticles of Hannah, Miriam, Deborah — now fulfilled and surpassed in the Mother of the incarnate Word.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Luke, Homily II (R. Payne Smith trans., Oxford: University Press, 1859). PD.",
