        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Luke</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;No room in the inn&#x27; — Cyril hears the verse as the canonical sign that the Word enters the world rejected from the start, foreshadowing the Cross&#x27;s final rejection. The manger is itself a eucharistic image: the food-trough of beasts becomes the resting-place of the Bread that comes down from heaven. Tewahedo Nativity hymnody draws directly on this Cyrillian reading of the manger as proto-altar.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Luke, Homily I on the Nativity (R. Payne Smith trans., Oxford: University Press, 1859). PD.",
