        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Luke</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>On Christ&#x27;s choice of the Twelve &#x27;whom also he named apostles&#x27; (Lk 6:13), Cyril reads the act-of-naming-twelve as the canonical Lukan anchor of the doctrine of apostolic foundation: the twelve are not crowd-volunteers but Christ-selected after a night of prayer (Lk 6:12). The number twelve corresponds typologically to the twelve patriarchs/tribes; the new Israel is constituted with apostolic foundation. Tewahedo episcopal theology cites Lk 6:13 as the canonical Lukan anchor of the apostolic origin of the episcopate — the bishop&#x27;s authority traces by laying-on-of-hands through unbroken succession to the apostolic Twelve.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Luke, Homily XLI (R. Payne Smith trans., 1859). PD.",
