        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Luke</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>On Christ&#x27;s &#x27;Be ye therefore merciful, as your Father also is merciful&#x27; (Lk 6:36), Cyril reads the Lukan be-merciful command as the distinctive Lukan parallel to Matthew&#x27;s &#x27;Be ye therefore perfect, as your Father which is in heaven is perfect&#x27; (Mt 5:48) — Luke&#x27;s choice of &#x27;merciful&#x27; (oiktirmones) rather than &#x27;perfect&#x27; (teleios) highlights the Father&#x27;s mercy as the defining attribute that Christian ethics imitates. Tewahedo soteriology cites Lk 6:36 + Mt 5:48 as the canonical doubled-witness for the theosis-pattern: Christian perfection IS divine mercy received and extended.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Luke, Homily XLV (R. Payne Smith trans., 1859). PD. Cf. Mt 5:48.",
