        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Luke</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>On Christ&#x27;s answer to JBaptist&#x27;s disciples &#x27;the blind see, the lame walk, the lepers are cleansed, the deaf hear, the dead are raised, to the poor the gospel is preached&#x27; (Lk 7:22), Cyril reads the sixfold sign-list as the canonical Lukan anchor of the doctrine that Christ&#x27;s identity is demonstrated by the Isaian Messianic signs (Is 35:5-6 + Is 61:1) — the same prophet whom John quoted at his preaching now points back to him. The signs are cumulative-eschatological: the Messianic age has arrived. Tewahedo christology cites Lk 7:22 + Is 35 + Is 61 as the canonical triple-witness of the prophetic-fulfillment evidence of Christ&#x27;s identity.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Luke, Homily XLVIII (R. Payne Smith trans., 1859). PD. Cf. Is 35:5-6, Is 61:1.",
