        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Luke</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Where is your faith?&#x27; — Christ&#x27;s rebuke to the terrified disciples in the storm is for Cyril the canonical anchor of the disciples&#x27; still-developing recognition of his divinity. The Word who rebukes the wind is the same Word who, in Job and the Psalms, treads upon the waves of the sea. The storm-stilling is a theophanic act, and the disciples&#x27; question &#x27;who then is this?&#x27; answers itself. Tewahedo Christology cites Lk 8:25 as a canonical anchor of the disciples&#x27; graduated confession of the Word&#x27;s divinity.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Luke, Homily XLIII (R. Payne Smith trans., Oxford: University Press, 1859). PD.",
