        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Luke</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>The blind beggar at Jericho — &#x27;Jesus, thou son of David, have mercy on me&#x27; — gives, for Cyril, the canonical short-form messianic address. The blind man sees by faith what the seeing crowd does not see: the Davidic sonship of the passing Christ. Tewahedo invocation of the Jesus-prayer preserves the blind-beggar address as one of its earliest canonical forms.</p></aside>',
