        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Luke</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>Christ&#x27;s weeping over Jerusalem is for Cyril the canonical disclosure of the Lord&#x27;s mercy precisely toward the city about to reject him. The tears do not soften the prophetic announcement of the city&#x27;s destruction; they intensify it as the announcement of a real and grievous loss. Cyril rejects every reading that would treat the tears as mere stagecraft. Tewahedo Holy-Week lectionary preserves Lk 19:41-44 as the Palm-Sunday-eve reading of the Lord&#x27;s lament.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Luke, Homily CXXVIII (R. Payne Smith trans., Oxford: University Press, 1859). PD.",
