        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Luke</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;This poor widow hath cast in more than they all&#x27; — Cyril reads the widow&#x27;s mite as the canonical anchor of the all-or-nothing form of Christian almsgiving: the gift is measured not by the amount given but by the proportion of one&#x27;s substance, and the widow who gives her last two coins gives literally everything. Tewahedo monastic voluntary poverty draws on Lk 21:3-4 as one of its earliest canonical anchors of total renunciation.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Luke, Homily CXXXVIII (R. Payne Smith trans., Oxford: University Press, 1859). PD.",
