        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Luke</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>On Christ&#x27;s &#x27;Watch ye therefore, and pray always, that ye may be accounted worthy to escape all these things that shall come to pass, and to stand before the Son of man&#x27; (Lk 21:36), Cyril reads the watch-and-pray-always + stand-before-the-Son-of-Man as the canonical Lukan anchor of the doctrine of eschatological-vigilance grounded in ceaseless-prayer (doubled with Lk 18:1 — &#x27;always to pray, and not to faint&#x27;). The stand-before-the-Son-of-Man is the canonical Lukan formula for eschatological-judgment-readiness. Tewahedo monastic-vigil-prayer (the night-office tradition of the great monasteries) cites Lk 21:36 + Lk 18:1 as the canonical doubled-Lukan-anchor for the ceaseless-prayer + eschatological-vigilance discipline.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Luke, Homily CXLII (R. Payne Smith trans., 1859). PD. Cf. Lk 18:1.",
