        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Luke</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>On Christ&#x27;s &#x27;This cup is the new testament in my blood, which is shed for you&#x27; (Lk 22:20), Cyril reads the new-testament-in-my-blood as the canonical Lukan anchor of the doctrine of the eucharistic-cup-as-new-covenant-blood: the Lord identifies the wine as the cup of the New-Covenant ratified by his impending blood-shedding. The pairing of the bread-body (Lk 22:19 — seed entry) and the cup-blood-covenant institutes the full eucharistic-form. Tewahedo Anaphora theology cites Lk 22:20 + 1 Cor 11:25 as the canonical doubled-witness for the doctrine of the cup as the new-covenant-blood; the Tewahedo Mass preserves Christ&#x27;s covenant-blood institution language verbatim in every Anaphora.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Luke, Homily CXLIV (R. Payne Smith trans., 1859). PD. Cf. 1 Cor 11:25.",
