        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Luke</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>On Christ&#x27;s &#x27;But I have prayed for thee, that thy faith fail not: and when thou art converted, strengthen thy brethren&#x27; (Lk 22:32), Cyril reads the doubled-promise (I-prayed-for-thee + strengthen-thy-brethren) as the canonical Lukan anchor of the doctrine of dominical-intercession + apostolic-fraternity: Christ&#x27;s High-Priestly intercession precedes the apostolic ministry; Peter&#x27;s restoration is the model for fraternal-strengthening after each apostolic failure. Tewahedo pastoral-theology of confession cites Lk 22:32 as the canonical Lukan anchor for the priestly post-confession ministry — the restored confessor strengthens his brethren by sharing his repentance-and-restoration testimony.</p></aside>',
