    (
        23,
        43,
        "c",
        "",
        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Luke</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Today shalt thou be with me in paradise&#x27; — Cyril reads the promise to the good thief as the canonical anchor of three doctrines: (1) Christ retains the prerogative of paradise even at the moment of his apparent defeat; (2) confession-from-the-cross suffices for salvation; (3) the saints enter paradise immediately at death and do not wait. The &#x27;today&#x27; rules out every reading that defers the saints&#x27; beatific reception to the Last Day alone. Tewahedo intermediate-state doctrine cites Lk 23:43 as a principal canonical anchor.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Luke, Homily CLI (R. Payne Smith trans., Oxford: University Press, 1859). PD.",
    ),
